/P 164 0 R
/T (Continuous Integration \(CI\) is the practice of merging changes frequently and validating them automatically. A CI pipeline may run formatting checks, unit tests, static analysis, dependency checks, and packaging. Quick feedback helps developers identify defects close to the change that introduced them. Required checks should prevent failed changes from progressing to release stages.)
/E (Continuous Integration \(CI\) is the practice of merging changes frequently and validating them automatically. A CI pipeline may run formatting checks, unit tests, static analysis, dependency checks, and packaging. Quick feedback helps developers identify defects close to the change that introduced them. Required checks should prevent failed changes from progressing to release stages.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
