/E (Security should be included throughout the delivery lifecycle. Use least-privilege IAM policies, short-lived credentials where possible, protected branches, reviewed pipeline changes, dependency checks, image scanning, and restricted network exposure. Secrets should be stored in an approved secret manager or CI credential store and injected at runtime. They should never be committed to source control or printed in pipeline logs.)
