528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (A maintainable repository separates application source, tests, container configuration, pipeline code, Kubernetes manifests, and documentation. A suggested structure is: app/ for application code; tests/ for automated tests; Dockerfile for image build instructions; Jenkinsfile for pipeline stages; k8s/ for deployment and service resources; monitoring/ for dashboards and alerts; and README.md for setup and recovery instructions.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 176 0 R
/T (4.2 Source Control Workflow)
/E (4.2 Source Control Workflow)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Create a feature branch for each change, commit focused updates, and open a pull request for review. Automated checks should run on the pull request. Merge only after required checks pass and approvals are complete. Use descriptive commit messages and release tags. Generated files, local environment files, and secrets should be excluded from the repository. 4.3 Application Health Endpoint)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
531 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (The application should expose a health endpoint that returns success when the service is ready to receive requests. The endpoint should not reveal environment variables, credentials, or internal infrastructure details. Logs should be written to standard output and standard error so container platforms can collect them. A readiness endpoint should reflect the ability to serve traffic, not merely that a process has started.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 176 0 R
/T (4.4 Configuration Management)
/E (4.4 Configuration Management)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Environment-specific settings should be kept separate from the application image. Non- sensitive values may be supplied through configuration resources, while secrets should be injected using a secure secret mechanism. Configuration changes should be reviewed and versioned. The same image can then be promoted through development, testing, and production with only approved environment configuration changing.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
