540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (The build process starts from a maintained base image, installs required dependencies, copies application files, and defines the startup command. A .dockerignore file excludes local dependencies, temporary output, version-control metadata, and environment files. Builds should be repeatable and should not depend on untracked local files.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 177 0 R
/T (4.6 Image Quality and Security)
/E (4.6 Image Quality and Security)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (Image quality checks can identify vulnerable packages, outdated base images, embedded secrets, excessive permissions, and unnecessary files. Images should be scanned according to project policy and rebuilt when important security fixes become available. The final runtime image should contain only the components required to run the service.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 177 0 R
/T (4.7 Image Tagging and Registry)
/E (4.7 Image Tagging and Registry)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
544 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (Each successful build should use a unique tag based on the source commit or release version. Avoid relying only on the mutable latest tag. Amazon ECR can store the image and apply repository permissions. The pipeline should verify that the image was published successfully before attempting deployment.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
545 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 177 0 R
/T (4.8 Local Verification)
/E (4.8 Local Verification)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (Before cloud deployment, run the container locally and confirm that the application starts, listens on the expected port, and responds to the health endpoint. Verify that environment variables are handled correctly and that logs are useful. A locally successful image is not proof of production readiness, but it provides an early validation step.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
