553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (The checkout stage retrieves the intended repository revision. The validation stage checks code formatting and configuration. The test stage executes unit and integration tests. The build stage creates the image using the selected Dockerfile. The publish stage authenticates to the registry and pushes a unique tag. The deploy stage updates the Kubernetes workload, and the verify stage confirms rollout and application health.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (4.10 Pipeline Quality Gates)
/E (4.10 Pipeline Quality Gates)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (A quality gate defines a condition that must be satisfied before a release proceeds. Examples include successful tests, an acceptable vulnerability scan result, successful image publication, and an approved deployment. A failed stage should stop later release actions and preserve logs. The pipeline should report a clear reason for failure rather than merely returning a generic error.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (4.11 Credential Handling)
/E (4.11 Credential Handling)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (Credentials should be managed through a CI credential store or an approved cloud identity mechanism. Avoid long-lived access keys when short-lived role-based access is available. Permissions should be restricted to the required registry and cluster resources. Pipeline logs should be checked to ensure tokens and secret values are masked and never echoed. 4.12 Deployment Verification)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (A successful command does not necessarily mean that users can access the application. Verification should check Kubernetes rollout status, Pod readiness, Service endpoints, and the health URL. Where possible, a smoke test should send a request through the same network path used by users. A failed verification should trigger an alert and a documented recovery decision.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
